PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
- The deliberation has consolidated into two primary candidates: Saint Sebastian and Walt Whitman.
- Saint Sebastian is the strongest candidate because the visual comparison of his arrow-pierced iconography across Western art to a porcupine directly explains the phrase "in all the pictures."
- The name Saint Sebastian satisfies the constraint of being a two-word designation starting with the letter S.
- In subsequent rounds, the focus will remain on reinforcing the literal visual match of Saint Sebastian against the photographic arguments for Walt Whitman.
}

